NAME
       truncate, ftruncate, fsync, fdatasync, sync - size and durability

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>

       int truncate(const char *path, off_t length);
       int ftruncate(int fd, off_t length);
       int fsync(int fd);
       int fdatasync(int fd);
       void sync(void);

DESCRIPTION
       truncate sets a file's size, extending it with zeroes or
       discarding the tail.

       fsync writes one file's data and metadata to the device;
       fdatasync skips metadata that does not affect reading the data
       back. sync flushes everything. Writes are buffered until then,
       so anything that must survive a power cut needs one of these.

RETURN VALUE
       0 on success, -1 with errno set.

ERRORS
       EBADF    fd is not open for writing
       EINVAL   the length is negative

SEE ALSO
       write(2), sync(1), open(2)
